From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:26:05 +0900
Subject: Check a refinement against the tracked value itself, not its widened
 type

Under capture checking a tracked value did not conform to a refinement of its
own type which mentions the value:

    def same(reader: Reader^): (Reader { type Topic = reader.Topic })^{reader} = reader

Against a capturing type, the comparer first accounts for the captures of the
left-hand side, here `{reader}`, and then compares what is left with the
parent of the right. For a singleton it tried two things: its widened type
with the capture set stripped, `Reader`, which no longer says which value it
is, so that `Topic = reader.Topic` cannot be shown; and the singleton as it
stands, which is not a subtype of the pure class beneath the refinement,
because its capture set, though already accounted for, is not empty. So the
conformance failed with "capability `any` cannot flow into capture set
{reader}", though it holds without capture checking.

Where the parent is a refined type, a singleton is now also compared in two
parts: its widened, stripped type with what lies beneath the refinements, and
each refinement with the member of the singleton itself.

Written with LLM assistance (Claude Code); reviewed content.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: refinedsingleton
---
 .../dotty/tools/dotc/core/TypeComparer.scala  | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 .../captures/refined-singleton.scala          | 12 ++++++++++++
 .../captures/refined-singleton.scala          | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 47 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/neg-custom-args/captures/refined-singleton.scala
 create mode 100644 tests/pos-custom-args/captures/refined-singleton.scala

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/TypeComparer.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/TypeComparer.scala
index 3f74b6dc4e913924a74a6bca12439829c616b99a..db8546820b28d265172eb9ef1a06b0b0a54b73d3 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/TypeComparer.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/TypeComparer.scala
@@ -893,12 +893,28 @@ class TypeComparer(@constructorOnly initctx: Context) extends ConstraintHandling
                     recur(tp1.widen, tp2)
                   case _ =>
                     false
+                // A refinement of `parent2` may mention the singleton `tp1` itself, as in
+                // `x: C^ <: C { type T = x.T }^{x}`. Its widened type no longer says which
+                // value it is, and `tp1` as it stands is not a subtype of the pure class
+                // under the refinement, since its capture set, already accounted for by
+                // `refs2`, is not empty. So compare the widened type with what is under
+                // the refinements, and each refinement with the member of `tp1` itself.
+                def refinedOK(tp1: SingletonType, parent2: Type): Boolean = parent2 match
+                  case parent2: RefinedType if !defn.isRefinedFunction(parent2) =>
+                    refinedOK(tp1, parent2.parent)
+                    && hasMatchingMember(parent2.refinedName, tp1, parent2)
+                  case _ =>
+                    recur(tp1.widen.stripCapturing, parent2)
+                def singletonRefinedOK = tp1 match
+                  case tp1: SingletonType => parent2.isInstanceOf[RefinedType] && refinedOK(tp1, parent2)
+                  case _ => false
                 singletonOK
                 || compareCaptures(tp1, refs1, tp2, refs2)
                     && (recur(tp1.widen.stripCapturing, parent2)
                       || tp1.isInstanceOf[SingletonType] && recur(tp1, parent2)
                           // this alternative is needed in case the right hand side is a
                           // capturing type that contains the lhs as an alternative of a union type.
+                      || singletonRefinedOK
                       )
           catch case ex: AssertionError =>
             println(i"assertion failed while compare captured $tp1 <:< $tp2")
diff --git a/tests/neg-custom-args/captures/refined-singleton.scala b/tests/neg-custom-args/captures/refined-singleton.scala
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c23f35116cb90f80fada871a4b8503db4c8e2fa4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/neg-custom-args/captures/refined-singleton.scala
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+import language.experimental.captureChecking
+
+// What tests/pos-custom-args/captures/refined-singleton.scala accepts must not extend
+// to a value whose capture set the expected type does not account for, or to a
+// refinement the value's own member does not meet.
+
+class Terrain
+abstract class Reader(val view: Terrain^) { type Topic; val terrain: Terrain^ }
+
+def pure(reader: Reader^): Reader { type Topic = reader.Topic } = reader // error
+def less(reader: Reader^, other: Reader^): (Reader { type Topic = reader.Topic })^{other} = reader // error
+def member(reader: Reader^): (Reader { val terrain: Terrain })^{reader} = reader // error
diff --git a/tests/pos-custom-args/captures/refined-singleton.scala b/tests/pos-custom-args/captures/refined-singleton.scala
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..75a4ce304616557acdd1fad2176e71e1c971fde1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/pos-custom-args/captures/refined-singleton.scala
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+import language.experimental.captureChecking
+
+// A tracked value conforms to a refinement of its type which mentions the value
+// itself. Its capture set is that of the expected type, or part of it, but the
+// refinement was then checked against the value's widened type, which no longer
+// says which value it is: "capability `any` cannot flow into capture set {reader}".
+
+class Terrain
+abstract class Reader(val view: Terrain^) { type Topic; val terrain: Terrain^ }
+
+def same(reader: Reader^): (Reader { type Topic = reader.Topic })^{reader} = reader
+
+def member(reader: Reader^)
+:   (Reader { type Topic = reader.Topic; val terrain: Terrain^{reader.terrain} })^{reader} =
+  reader
+
+def function(reader: Reader^): Int =
+  val read: (Reader { type Topic = reader.Topic })^ => Int = _ => 0
+  read(reader)
